<title>BELGIUM: Belgium edges liquidity up at money tender.</title>
<headline>Belgium edges liquidity up at money tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank slightly raised money market liquidity at its fixed-rate tender for seven-day advances. Details -</p>
<p>    Value date 28/05	  expiry on 04/06    NBVA</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	   15.050 bln bfr    (15.000 bln *)</p>
<p>    Interest rate	     3.00 pct	    (3.00 pct **)</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids    139.550 bln bfr</p>
<p>Percentage of bids accepted  10.63</p>
<p>* amount draining from the money market on 28/05</p>
<p>** interest rate at previous tender on 16/05</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
